commit 3c851d23ab7983ae871c1c92b0d234215ead9ade
Author: poupou97 <nbp85hn@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Jul 30 15:40:18 2026 +0700

    fix(WTM-146): P0 §3 — test governance: literal ratchet, fallback kill, real-DB restart, overflow + nav suites (#71)
    
    Production fixes (2 real bugs found by the new suites):
    - SampleDataSeeder.removeAll deleted customers BEFORE orders → FOREIGN KEY
      787 on the real SQLite database (PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON); in-memory test
      doubles never enforced it — the exact §1 bug class. Orders now delete first
      (ADR-TON-014 updated).
    - Home overflowed at 320px/1.3x text scale (health badge, module tiles,
      section-header action) — Flexible+FittedBox fixes.
    
    Hardening:
    - Kill the two remaining silent .sample() fallbacks in UI (Reports
      metrics-only branch, Customer history bare-construct) → empty, never
      fixtures
    - Bottom-nav labels + ~180 remaining EN-literal chrome strings (20 screens,
      More entries incl. new stable Keys) → context.l10n keys; AppStrings now
      ~290 keys VI/EN
    - Stable Keys for More entries (more-language/ai-key/timeline/finance/
      reports/goals/export)
    
    New P0 governance suites (test/features/tongtai/p0/):
    - localization_test: final ratchet — NO string literal in ANY ui/ text
      position (allowlist: product names; dev-only showcase excluded)
    - sample_fallback_scan_test: .sample() banned in ui/ (allowlist: curated
      supplier catalog, Phase-2 by design)
    - l10n_placeholder_test: every parameterized string interpolates all args
      in both locales
    - nav_availability_test: 5 tabs render+switch, full More entry list and
      create paths in EVERY data state (real app shell wiring)
    - overflow_test: no RenderFlex overflow @320px/1.3x vi+en, empty+seeded;
      2.0x long-content proxy
    - drift_restart_test: full sample lifecycle across 3 AppDatabase sessions
      on one real .db file
    
    Evidence: flutter analyze clean · 990/990 tests pass
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

